Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||02-22-2000||04:42 AM||||Supposedly, the cookie problem should've been solved with the latest version of the forum's software (which was installed a few days ago). Try this:<P>- Click <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/ubbmisc.cgi?action=clearcookies" TARGET=_blank>here</A><BR>- Close Netscape<BR>- Open Netscape<BR>- Check the forum again<P>If it still doesn't work, I just might change the software myself to get those darn cookies working. It's just the way this software implements cookies  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> - using Javascript which is being less and less supported by browsers. There's another (much better) way to set cookies - it's just a lot of work to implement.||||reg||1
